    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d516">

                <pb facs="0699" n="600" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg600"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/3129: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gordon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-04-03T13:00:00-05:00">April 3, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>18. Department’s instruction No. 360 of February 4. Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs<anchor n="5" xml:id="d516-f1"/> this morning under instructions from
                    the President sounded me out on the possibilities of signing the proposed new
                    treaty terminating financial control. He said that with the opposition becoming
                    increasingly active as the day of his second inauguration on May 15th
                    approaches, the President would like to announce this last step in the
                    attainment of total liberation.</p>
                <p>I replied that the President already had very substantial concrete achievements
                    to boast of and that the present moment, especially <pb facs="0700" n="601"
                        xml:id="pg601"/> when he was seeking a loan on the American market, would be
                    a most unfortunate one to raise the question. Amplifying despatch by air
                    mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gordon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d516-f1" n="5" xml:id="d516-f1-content">
                <p>Yrech Chetelain.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
